HotkeyString.mcc/HotkeyString.mcc

    NAME
        HotkeyString.mcc -- Capture a textual key description.

    SUPERCLASS
        BetterString.mcc

    DESCRIPTION
        Represent captured raw-key input as String_Contents. This source
        defines version 12.28. The class does not register a global hotkey,
        execute a command, or return a parsed InputXpression. The application
        validates, stores, and uses the description.
        Setup adds a priority-1 raw-key event handler alongside the inherited
        BetterString handler. Capture through this handler requires Active and
        Snoop. Key-up events and next/previous-gadget navigation are not
        captured. Unhandled HandleEvent messages return zero rather than being
        forwarded directly; inherited input handling uses its separately
        registered handler.
        Qualifier names appear in this order: lshift, rshift, capslock,
        control, lalt, ralt, lcommand, rcommand, numericpad, repeat.
        Modifier-only input can produce just this text; higher qualifier bits
        are not represented. Named keys include arrows,
        function/navigation/media keys and supported wheel events. Other keys
        use one unqualified keymap byte, with names for backspace, tab,
        return/enter, esc, space, and del. This is not lossless serialization
        of every input event.

    NOTES
        Contents changes pass through BetterString and its notification
        handling. Capture does not automatically turn Snoop off. Successive
        captured Backspace inputs alternate between a backspace description
        and an empty string; another recognized key resets this toggle. An
        unmapped key can be consumed without changing content.
        Active capture overwrites Window_DisableKeys. Disabling capture or
        leaving active capture writes zero rather than restoring an earlier
        application mask. Coordinate that window-wide setting with other
        controls and use matched Setup/Cleanup to remove the extra handler.
        Read String_Contents for borrowed text and copy it before editing or
        disposal. Neither own attribute has a local getter. Version and
        Revision do. BetterString ownership, byte-string and editing
        limitations also apply.

    COPYRIGHT
        Copyright (C) 2005-2018 BetterString.mcc Open Source Team
